<worksheet >
    <title>IC-4 Change of Variables</title>
  <introduction>
    <p> To earn an M on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete 
      both parts. To earn a P on this outcome, you will need to correctly 
      complete the first part with progress on the second.</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise>
        <introduction><p>Given the integral <m>\iint_R \frac{x-2y}{3x+y} dA</m> 
          where <m>R</m> is the trapezoidal region with vertices 
          <m>(1,0), (4,0), (0,4)</m> and <m>(0,1)</m>.</p></introduction>
        <task  workspace="2.5in"><statement><p>Set up a change of variables and find the Jacobian.</p></statement></task>
        <task  workspace="2.0in"><statement><p>Evaluate the integral.</p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>